  "question": {
    "text": "If $5 \\cos 2 \\theta+2 \\cos ^2 \\frac{\\theta}{2}+1=0$, when $(0 < \\theta < \\pi)$, then the values of $\\theta$ are :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3} \\pm \\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right) \\pm \\pi$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\pi-\\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints : $5 \\cos 2 \\theta+1+\\cos \\theta+1=0$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& 5\\left(2 \\cos ^2 \\theta-1\\right)+\\cos \\theta+2=0 \\\\\n& 10 \\cos ^2 \\theta+\\cos \\theta-3=0 \\\\\n& (5 \\cos \\theta+3)(2 \\cos \\theta-1)=0 \\\\\n& \\cos \\theta=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n& \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n$$\n\\mid \\begin{aligned}\n& \\cos \\theta=-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\\n& \\theta=\\cos ^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{3}{5}\\right) \\\\\n& =\\pi-\\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
